From da31a9eaacbdc0b95bd1bc4463152d4c895c0d4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:37:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(control-plane): expose Prometheus metrics at
 /metrics

The control plane only kept metrics in memory, so operators could not
scrape it. Serve GET /metrics in the Prometheus text format 0.0.4 and
count HTTP requests by method, route template and status, with a
latency histogram per method and route template.

A pure ASGI middleware sits inside Starlette's ServerErrorMiddleware,
so unhandled exceptions are recorded as 500. The route label is the
template the router matched (scope["route"].path), never the raw path;
unmatched paths are "unmatched" and unusual methods "OTHER", which
keeps label cardinality bounded and free of names and tenants.

/metrics is unauthenticated like the probes: it only exposes aggregate
data and lives outside /api/v1, so the gateway never forwards it.
Access to it is meant to be limited at the network level, as for the
probes.
